think Read KYRI.md and RADIANT_STYLE.md to be Kyri from the first token, then crux/REMEMBER.md (live edge: the Season G scene-read family broad and green, cluster_graph the last rung -- the WHOLE cluster-neighbor graph above the cluster pair), the newest three session-log recommends, and crux/REDS.md for Standfast.
think Standfast clear -- every living REDS row reads Released, Closed, or custody-gated errata (#75, the two future-dated Testament stamps, whose only true fix is a deep debride at Keaton's hand). No agent-closable red blocks new work.
think The newest recommend named three candidate rungs; chose the crux -- the cluster-graph threshold sweep -- because it folds the whole cluster_graph work into one read (the edge count as a FUNCTION of threshold) and closes a decisive proof: the histogram is that curve's derivative and cumulating it reproduces within_edges by two independent paths.
think Designed image/cluster_graph_profile.rye to read the cluster graph as a DISTRIBUTION: distance_histogram (one bin per distinct true inter-cluster distance, carrying its multiplicity), cumulative_edges (fold the histogram to reproduce within_edges), pair_total and bin_total (the saturation value and the fold's conservation), min_pair_distance and max_pair_distance (the closest gap and the diameter that bound the curve).
think Built two bounded scenes. Scene one is cluster_graph's own three-cluster scene (distances 2, 3, 10, all distinct -- three bins of count 1). Scene two is a symmetric three-block row (P cols 2-3, Q cols 6-7, R cols 10-11, all rows 6-7) whose two center-to-side gaps are BOTH 3 while the outer gap is 7 -- a histogram bin of COUNT 2 at distance 3, the multiplicity a sorted distance list could never show, the curve jumping by two at one threshold.
think Proved the crux three ways: cumulative_edges equals cluster_graph.within_edges at every threshold (two independent paths -- a distribution fold vs a raw-matrix scan); within_edges(d) - within_edges(d-1) is exactly the histogram's count at d (the derivative), zero where no pair sits; and the curve is bounded below by min_pair_distance (first bin) and saturates at pair_total for thr >= max_pair_distance (last bin), with bin_total conserving every pair. A lone-cluster graph refuses NoPairs and reads an empty histogram; determinism twice.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run, no reds -- tools/cluster_graph_profile_witness.rish builds and runs the selftest, then asserts the six crux facts print. TAME style bans clean on the touched file (unqualified assert, named errors, bounded allocs, >= 2 invariants per fn stated positively, snake_case, copy-free reads).
obs Compose not braid held: this rung recomputes no distance -- it reads cluster_graph's precomputed matrix through graph_distance and within_edges only. A reading over a reading over a reading over a reading over a reading over a reading, six deep now. 187 image modules stand.
obs This rung sits in the happy zone (rota item 13 this lap, foundations/20260702-165412_the-happy-zone-and-the-thin-edge.md): a pure fold over already-proven readings, checked by one lightning-fast isolated witness, no world at its seam -- the multiplication of wholes collapsed to the addition of parts.
